From 22a87993dd1916d21f9b3bed332c342f39607098 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Sandfort <eriksandfort@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:47:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm: fall back to the GBM platform when no EGL device matches

CDRMRenderer::attempt(backend, drmFD) resolves a renderer through
EGL_PLATFORM_DEVICE_EXT, which requires an EGL device that matches the
DRM node. Devices that expose KMS without a render node have no such
match: eglQueryDeviceStringEXT returns EGL_BAD_PARAMETER for them, so
eglDeviceFromDRMFD finds nothing and renderer creation fails.

initMgpu() gave up at that point even though the GBM-platform overload,
CDRMRenderer::attempt(backend, allocator), initializes fine on these
devices, and initMgpu() has already built the allocator it needs. Try
it before failing.

Failing also had no memory. updateSecondaryRendererState() runs from
applyCommit, so every commit re-entered initMgpu(), reopened the DRM
node, built a fresh GBM allocator and re-ran the whole EGL enumeration.
On a VirtualBox guest (vboxvideo, no render node) that logged four
errors and the full EGL client-extension string per commit: ~20 failed
commits/sec writing 17 KB/s, 59 MB/hour into /run. Because the retry
sits inline on the commit path, it also delays every frame. When both
paths fail, stop requiring a renderer instead of retrying forever.

This generalizes two existing narrow fixes in the same area. #291 falls
back to the sole renderD node when parent-syspath matching fails, which
cannot help when the device has no render node at all, and the
AQ_BACKEND_GPU_DRIVER_EVDI case hardcodes one driver name. Devices
still falling through include vboxvideo, vmwgfx without 3D, qxl and
simpledrm.

Tested on VirtualBox 7.2.16 / vboxvideo with no renderD node: the GBM
fallback now creates a renderer (llvmpipe, OpenGL ES 3.2) where none
was created before, and the per-commit error storm is gone.
---
 src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp b/src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp
index 431c83fa..0c9980e1 100644
--- a/src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp
@@ -877,8 +877,21 @@ bool Aquamarine::CDRMBackend::initMgpu() {
 
     rendererState.renderer = CDRMRenderer::attempt(backend.lock(), gpu->renderNodeFd >= 0 ? gpu->renderNodeFd : gpu->fd);
 
+    if (!rendererState.renderer) {
+        // KMS-only devices (VM display adapters such as vboxvideo, DisplayLink, simpledrm)
+        // expose no EGL device matching their DRM node, so the EGL_PLATFORM_DEVICE path
+        // above finds nothing. EGL_PLATFORM_GBM still initializes on them, so try it
+        // before giving up.
+        backend->log(AQ_LOG_DEBUG, "drm: initMgpu: no EGL device matches this DRM node, trying the GBM platform");
+        rendererState.renderer = CDRMRenderer::attempt(backend.lock(), newAllocator);
+    }
+
     if (!rendererState.renderer) {
         backend->log(AQ_LOG_ERROR, "drm: initMgpu: no renderer");
+        // Nothing about this GPU changes until it is re-registered, so a retry cannot
+        // succeed. Stop requiring a renderer; otherwise every commit repeats the whole
+        // attempt, which costs tens of milliseconds of CPU per frame and floods the log.
+        rendererRequired = false;
         return false;
     }
 
@@ -1542,6 +1555,8 @@ void Aquamarine::CDRMBackend::onReady() {
             backend->log(AQ_LOG_ERROR, "drm: onReady: no renderer for gl formats");
         else {
             auto r = CDRMRenderer::attempt(backend.lock(), gpu->renderNodeFd >= 0 ? gpu->renderNodeFd : gpu->fd);
+            if (!r)
+                r = CDRMRenderer::attempt(backend.lock(), a); // KMS-only device: no matching EGL device, but GBM works
             if (!r)
                 backend->log(AQ_LOG_ERROR, "drm: onReady: no renderer for gl formats");
             else {
